52 \cdot 27 = 1404
\] Finding \( 1404 \pmod{55} \): \[
1404 \div 55 = 25 \text{ remainder } 19
\] So: \[
r \equiv 19 \pmod{55}
\] The least positive four-digit solution of \( r \) is: \[
